WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>OSHI NO KO</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

01:29.990 --> 01:34.200
<b>North Exit Shopping Arcade
Hula Dance Club
Private Audition
Sunflower R&R
Yasuoka</b>

01:31.550 --> 01:33.740
Okay, your turn next, Ruby.

01:34.680 --> 01:38.910
<i>If this were any other audition, 
Ruby-chan wouldn't stand a chance.</i>

01:39.180 --> 01:41.850
<i>So there must be a reason 
she's a part of this,</i>

01:42.520 --> 01:45.330
<i>and I'm betting it has to do 
with this role—this movie.</i>

01:45.840 --> 01:47.290
Say, Ruby.

01:47.550 --> 01:50.760
What does lying mean to you?

01:53.390 --> 01:55.380
<i>I have to play a liar?</i>

01:59.680 --> 02:02.560
<i>What makes a lie... What makes a liar?</i>

02:03.190 --> 02:05.520
<i>Does acting count as lying?</i>

02:07.560 --> 02:09.290
<i>I'm good at acting.</i>

02:09.290 --> 02:10.690
<i>So much so,</i>

02:10.690 --> 02:14.310
<i>Aqua even thought it was in my future 
back when we were babies.</i>

02:15.760 --> 02:16.650
<i>After all...</i>

02:17.400 --> 02:19.490
<i>I'm acting all the time,</i>

02:20.400 --> 02:22.590
<i>playing the role of "Ruby Hoshino."</i>

02:23.350 --> 02:26.520
<i>Trying to live up to the role 
of Ai Hoshino's daughter,</i>

02:27.270 --> 02:31.890
<i>a cheerful, innocent, and genuine idol 
who has overcome her mother's death.</i>

02:33.310 --> 02:37.460
<i>Because I think that's what 
Mom hoped I'd grow up to be.</i>

02:42.070 --> 02:44.760
<i>I was acting all the time,</i>

02:46.010 --> 02:48.270
<i>playing the role of "Sarina Tendouji."</i>

02:49.790 --> 02:55.110
<i>Who didn't resent her parents for being 
too busy to visit her in the hospital—</i>

02:55.810 --> 02:58.160
<i>a brave yet pitiful girl.</i>

02:59.600 --> 03:04.880
<i>I had to, 'cause I was too powerless to do
anything without the help of other people,</i>

03:06.010 --> 03:08.710
<i>and I knew that was 
the only way I could survive.</i>

03:10.570 --> 03:14.470
<i>So I hid all of the ugly emotions 
inside of the real me.</i>

03:16.220 --> 03:19.250
<i>Was it like that for Mom, too?</i>

03:20.640 --> 03:24.950
<i>She played the perfect idol, 
hiding the fact she had kids.</i>

03:25.350 --> 03:29.210
<i>She was always cheerful and carefree.</i>

03:32.110 --> 03:35.480
<i>But was that all an act?</i>

03:36.470 --> 03:39.810
<i>Did she bottle up all her feelings inside?</i>

03:41.340 --> 03:43.650
<i>If she was the same as I am now—</i>

03:45.230 --> 03:47.040
<i>if she was a liar too, then...</i>

03:50.530 --> 03:51.670
It hurts.

03:52.270 --> 03:54.570
I hate it all. It sucks.

03:54.570 --> 03:56.690
Totally ridiculous. Why even?

03:56.690 --> 03:58.340
Irritating. I can't stand it.

03:58.340 --> 04:00.300
I envy you all. It's gross.

04:00.300 --> 04:01.510
It's awful! It hurts!

04:04.950 --> 04:09.100
I still have nightmares 
about the day Mom died.

04:10.060 --> 04:12.800
Why is Sensei dead, too?!

04:13.690 --> 04:18.400
Does everyone I come to love have to die?

04:18.880 --> 04:20.970
I'm too scared to love anybody.

04:21.940 --> 04:25.410
I wanna join them where they are.

04:26.810 --> 04:29.370
I want to die.

04:33.700 --> 04:34.940
Just kidding!

04:35.300 --> 04:38.000
That's totally not how I feel!

04:38.000 --> 04:39.990
I've gotten over it all, okay?

04:40.670 --> 04:41.800
That's all from me.

04:43.200 --> 04:46.640
Uh, that was... Yeah, okay.

04:47.150 --> 04:49.050
What do you say, Kurokawa-san?

04:49.050 --> 04:50.770
Yeah, that was good.

04:51.360 --> 04:56.690
I could nitpick it all day long, 
but she'll do just fine with training.

04:56.690 --> 04:58.740
Picky about acting, much?

04:59.150 --> 05:00.200
Okay.

05:00.630 --> 05:03.320
Let me pick up where she left off.

05:19.800 --> 05:21.260
Yay!

05:22.510 --> 05:26.600
Is that what's going on here, Frill-chan?

05:27.030 --> 05:29.180
What do you mean?

05:29.180 --> 05:33.190
Please. You're the biggest liar here.

05:33.760 --> 05:38.150
You wanted this role 
to go to Ruby all along, right?

05:38.670 --> 05:43.360
You're doing this to take me, 
the second choice, out of the running.

05:43.670 --> 05:44.950
What're you talking about?

05:45.890 --> 05:48.910
I'm just guessing here, 
but this little audition?

05:48.910 --> 05:52.190
I think it's to decide 
who plays Ai Hoshino.

05:53.280 --> 05:58.970
The movie Director Gotanda's making 
is based on Ai Hoshino's life.

05:58.970 --> 06:00.010
Am I wrong?

06:00.580 --> 06:02.160
What makes you believe that?

06:02.780 --> 06:05.680
Because it feels like the kind of thing 
Aqua-kun would think up.

06:06.470 --> 06:08.870
Consequences mean nothing to him anymore.

06:08.870 --> 06:13.120
He'll go to any lengths to reach his goal,
 even if it turns everyone against him.

06:14.300 --> 06:18.150
What, Aqua's using Mom as a cash grab now?

06:18.630 --> 06:21.610
Huh? I don't think that's 
what this is about.

06:22.270 --> 06:25.820
I mean, I couldn't believe my eyes 
when I read the script.

06:26.350 --> 06:30.160
I'd never in my life seen one with so 
much malice exuding from every page.

06:32.000 --> 06:37.460
I'm not totally stupid, so I realized 
what Aqua-san was doing.

06:37.700 --> 06:40.460
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

06:37.910 --> 06:40.460
He's making this movie for revenge.

06:40.860 --> 06:42.840
Him and Director Gotanda both.

06:45.980 --> 06:47.160
Aqua is...?

06:48.660 --> 06:54.200
As Kurokawa-san guessed, this movie 
is an account of Ai Hoshino-san's life.

06:54.640 --> 06:59.610
At the same time, it's also intended 
to condemn her killer.

06:59.930 --> 07:04.070
But the way I see it, that part's 
up to how Ai's actor plays the role.

07:05.790 --> 07:10.800
It all rests on whether she chooses 
to forgive her killer or not.

07:11.690 --> 07:17.040
So what matters is, 
who can best portray Ai-san's will?

07:17.040 --> 07:18.440
Mom's will...

07:20.790 --> 07:23.420
That makes me the only choice.

07:24.000 --> 07:29.090
I've profiled Ai-san, and I have 
a good grasp on her emotional quirks.

07:29.090 --> 07:33.470
I fully believe that I could express 
whatever she wanted to say.

07:34.340 --> 07:39.210
You have no acting experience, Ruby-chan. 
Do you think you could do better than me?

07:39.210 --> 07:40.310
I don't.

07:41.140 --> 07:42.020
But...

07:42.350 --> 07:45.150
Only I get how Mom felt.

07:45.670 --> 07:49.410
Nobody but me could understand her pain!

07:50.330 --> 07:53.490
I'm gonna be the one 
to avenge Mom and Sensei.

07:54.170 --> 07:57.540
It wouldn't be right 
for anybody else to do it!

07:57.940 --> 07:59.430
It has to be me.

08:01.120 --> 08:03.920
I don't like playing Aqua's games,

08:03.920 --> 08:07.380
and I was resigned to losing this 
until a minute ago.

08:07.380 --> 08:09.090
But things have changed.

08:09.370 --> 08:10.720
We're doing this until I win.

08:10.720 --> 08:12.550
Until I've convinced you both,

08:12.550 --> 08:14.180
I'm gonna give it my everything!

08:19.310 --> 08:22.060
<i>Awkward!</i>

08:22.060 --> 08:28.340
<i>This is a girl who saw me as a big sis—
the girl whose own mom got killed!</i>

08:28.340 --> 08:33.500
<i>How am I supposed to tell her I understand 
her mother better than she does?</i>

08:33.500 --> 08:36.540
<i>I don't have the nerve for that!</i>

08:36.950 --> 08:38.370
<i>And heck...</i>

08:37.750 --> 08:42.210
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

08:38.370 --> 08:42.210
<i>If I just want to be in the movie, 
it doesn't have to be as Ai.</i>

08:42.210 --> 08:44.430
That's what I wanted to hear!

08:44.430 --> 08:47.960
If you're that determined, 
you'll get through all the training!

08:47.960 --> 08:49.200
Akane-chan!

08:49.970 --> 08:52.310
<i>Can we just say that and wrap it all up?</i>

08:52.930 --> 08:54.400
Okay, let's do this!

08:56.790 --> 08:57.800
<i>After that,</i>

08:58.790 --> 09:01.920
<i>the audition went on 
until everyone was satisfied.</i>

09:02.810 --> 09:05.940
<i>Kurokawa-san's acting 
lacked its usual impact,</i>

09:06.280 --> 09:09.520
<i>and I was backing Ruby all along,</i>

09:10.230 --> 09:15.080
<i>so the private audition ended with us 
agreeing to let Ruby have the role.</i>

09:16.420 --> 09:18.580
Okay, good night.

09:18.580 --> 09:20.330
Night.

09:21.100 --> 09:24.420
Akane-chan, Frill-chan, 
I'll do my best to live up to your hopes!

09:24.710 --> 09:26.120
O-Okay...

09:35.960 --> 09:40.150
<i>Now I know all too well why auditions 
don't happen without the showrunners.</i>

09:40.640 --> 09:44.860
<i>You never get anywhere without 
someone to make the final call.</i>

09:42.510 --> 09:44.860
One more time! One more time!

09:45.640 --> 09:50.000
<i>Still, Ruby-chan's acting 
got better with each attempt.</i>

09:50.960 --> 09:54.120
<i>I guess you never know where you'll 
run into someone with real talent.</i>

09:55.410 --> 09:59.870
<i>When I turn down Ai's role, 
I'll sound them out about a different one.</i>

09:59.870 --> 10:01.370
<i>That way,</i>

10:01.800 --> 10:03.830
<i>I can still accomplish my goal.</i>

10:04.390 --> 10:07.790
<i>I won't let Aqua-kun have his way.</i>

10:08.130 --> 10:09.290
Are you done?

10:12.280 --> 10:13.640
It's been a while.

10:14.960 --> 10:17.930
I thought you were going to 
get out of my life forever?

10:18.240 --> 10:20.680
That was the idea,

10:21.770 --> 10:24.720
but I don't have the power 
to pick and choose the cast.

10:25.460 --> 10:26.350
Yeah?

10:28.790 --> 10:32.090
If you just want to make a movie, 
I'll gladly help out.

10:32.630 --> 10:37.160
But if you're planning to take it 
further than that by yourself,

10:37.660 --> 10:39.240
I <i>will</i> stop you.

10:40.990 --> 10:42.120
Oh, yeah?

10:49.870 --> 10:53.360
I'd love to see you try, Akane Kurokawa!

