11:29.960 --> 11:34.920
<b>MEMcho Fan</b>

11:29.960 --> 11:34.920
<b>Kana Arima Fan</b>

11:29.960 --> 11:34.920
<b>Kana Arima Fan</b>

11:29.960 --> 11:34.920
<b>Ruby Fan</b>

11:29.960 --> 11:34.920
<b>Ruby Fan</b>

11:37.870 --> 11:38.890
Ah-kun.

11:39.400 --> 11:40.570
What?

11:40.570 --> 11:42.580
Talk about something fun.

11:44.740 --> 11:47.900
How about the fact that 
Kana Arima is a panda?

11:47.900 --> 11:49.190
Say what?

11:49.570 --> 11:55.000
In the Himalayas in 1825, a westerner 
saw a lesser panda for the first time.

11:55.650 --> 11:57.860
He asked a local Nepalese man,

11:57.860 --> 12:00.000
"What is that?"

12:00.000 --> 12:02.830
And the Nepalese man told him 
it was a "nigalya ponya."

12:03.580 --> 12:07.200
"Ponya" got corrupted 
into the current word "panda."

12:07.200 --> 12:09.790
Now, as for what "nigalya ponya" 
actually means...

12:10.480 --> 12:12.920
It means "bamboo eater."

12:13.780 --> 12:14.840
Therefore,

12:15.510 --> 12:18.760
Kana Arima, who's eating bamboo 
shoots right now, is a panda.

12:18.760 --> 12:19.680
Wow!

12:19.940 --> 12:21.350
Eighty-four points!

12:21.350 --> 12:22.800
Glad you liked it.

12:23.390 --> 12:27.860
You know a lot about so many things. 
You're like Quiz*nock.

12:26.660 --> 12:27.620
Peep!

12:27.860 --> 12:29.520
It's not that big a deal.

12:29.930 --> 12:34.270
By the way, the word originally referred 
to what we now call the lesser panda,

12:34.270 --> 12:38.420
but after the black-and-white 
version got famous in 1869,

12:38.420 --> 12:41.870
the name was split between 
the lesser panda and the giant panda.

12:42.160 --> 12:44.940
FYI, lesser means inferior.

12:44.940 --> 12:46.580
Now you're even talking like them.

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>March
Schedule</b>

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>A business garbage disposal truck will be coming at 2 PM
on March 9th. Please collect and sort out your trash by then.</b>

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>Graduation
Certificate</b>

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>Take us along on
your graduation trip!</b>

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>To Hokkaido</b>

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>Or to Kyushu</b>

12:50.540 --> 12:55.750
<b>Baking Soda-senpai,
congrats on graduating high school!</b>

12:51.290 --> 12:54.800
Sure sounds like showbiz to me.

12:55.300 --> 12:58.850
The more popular ones 
take your name and legitimacy,

12:55.750 --> 13:01.220
<b>Yearly Music Ranking
1st Place
B-Komachi</b>

12:58.850 --> 13:01.220
and if you don't sell, 
you're called lesser?

13:01.950 --> 13:06.350
Reminds me of entertainers who 
couldn't become marquee attractions.

13:06.350 --> 13:07.880
Maybe so.

13:10.670 --> 13:13.300
I saw your post, by the way.

13:13.300 --> 13:14.190
Oh.

13:14.830 --> 13:19.150
I went and announced it. 
Now there's no going back.

13:19.670 --> 13:21.290
How time flies.

13:21.290 --> 13:25.620
It's been two years since you asked me 
to be an idol—two whole years.

13:26.180 --> 13:28.950
Sorry I was so pushy about it.

13:29.360 --> 13:30.080
Don't be.

13:30.850 --> 13:33.290
At this point, I'm grateful.

13:35.090 --> 13:41.510
If you hadn't done that, Kana Arima 
would've been dead as an entertainer.

13:42.320 --> 13:46.320
I would've been chilling in some 
not-bad, not-great college by now.

13:46.740 --> 13:49.270
Sounds like the safer bet to me.

13:49.270 --> 13:54.970
Who knows? Show business has always 
been a gambling den for social misfits.

13:54.970 --> 13:58.160
You never know if you win big 
or lose bad until you take that chance.

14:00.190 --> 14:04.190
I may have ended up quitting B-Komachi...

14:12.640 --> 14:17.250
But the experience helped me feel 
it was okay to bet on myself some more.

14:18.030 --> 14:21.840
Being part of B-Komachi was a lot of fun.

14:22.470 --> 14:24.840
Don't get me wrong! 
It was also a hard time!

14:25.430 --> 14:30.140
But hard times were all I'd had for ages, 
so it gave me hope again.

14:31.090 --> 14:35.320
I'm going to win big in this gamble 
and become a big-time panda.

14:36.350 --> 14:38.440
They're not going to call me "lesser."

14:40.390 --> 14:41.350
You do that.

14:42.790 --> 14:47.360
By the way, the director sent me 
an offer for that movie.

14:47.360 --> 14:51.390
I was offered the role of an original 
B-Komachi member who hates Ai.

14:52.370 --> 14:54.330
I'm taking it. That okay with you?

14:55.360 --> 15:00.220
Acting or not, I'll be talking all kinds 
of shit about your mom. You don't mind?

15:01.730 --> 15:03.420
If it's you, I don't mind.

15:03.760 --> 15:06.720
If it's me? Why?

15:07.530 --> 15:10.940
Because you're special to me. That's why.

15:14.310 --> 15:15.120
Huh?

15:15.600 --> 15:16.810
Wha?!

15:16.810 --> 15:19.820
What's that even mean? 
I'm not special or anything!

15:19.820 --> 15:21.020
That makes no sense!

15:21.020 --> 15:23.740
Gah! I'm gonna go buy us some drinks!

15:25.200 --> 15:28.340
<i>I'm trying to play it cool 
as a friend here!</i>

15:28.340 --> 15:30.340
<i>Why does he have to say 
such misleading things?!</i>

15:30.340 --> 15:31.870
<i>Is he stupid? Tactless moron!</i>

15:31.870 --> 15:35.040
<i>Does he actually like me or something?!</i>

15:40.740 --> 15:44.410
All I did was say something kinda smooth, 
and she completely lost it.

15:46.900 --> 15:50.820
Learn to doubt people 
a bit more, Kana Arima.

15:51.300 --> 15:56.230
If you let people like me tie you 
down and exploit you forever,

15:58.210 --> 16:00.410
someday you'll have nothing left to give.

16:04.920 --> 16:08.230
<i>The main cast's coming together 
one after another.</i>

16:09.170 --> 16:12.640
<i>We might be able to finalize the schedule 
all the way up to the start of filming.</i>

16:13.470 --> 16:14.870
<i>That said...</i>

16:16.990 --> 16:19.580
Ruby Hoshino's playing the lead, huh?

16:21.190 --> 16:27.220
<i>Failing to land either Frill Shiranui or 
Akane Kurokawa for the lead was a blow.</i>

16:27.870 --> 16:32.350
<i>Their schedules "only have room 
for a supporting role," huh?</i>

16:33.230 --> 16:35.970
<i>I doubt I can take that at face value.</i>

16:37.030 --> 16:41.170
<i>The director and Aqua-kun both 
seem to have an axe to grind, too.</i>

16:41.170 --> 16:44.010
<i>And I can more or less guess what it is.</i>

16:44.820 --> 16:48.400
<i>Is it condemnation? Vengeance?</i>

16:49.640 --> 16:52.550
<i>Or something even more?</i>

16:54.940 --> 16:57.450
Right now, Ruby Hoshino 
is the most pressing issue.

16:57.450 --> 17:01.960
We need her to become 
a real marquee attraction.

17:29.690 --> 17:32.280
What are you thinking about?

17:33.700 --> 17:37.020
Your sister? Your ex?

17:37.020 --> 17:39.630
The girl who's in love with you?

17:40.870 --> 17:43.780
Or your mother, maybe?

17:45.750 --> 17:48.660
You came to run your mouth at me again?

17:48.660 --> 17:50.170
Are you mad at me?

17:50.670 --> 17:55.760
Is it because I told you that Ai Hoshino 
no longer exists in this world?

17:55.760 --> 17:58.100
Shut up, you pest.

17:58.420 --> 18:01.810
Well, a part of you 
still held hope, right?

18:02.150 --> 18:05.220
That maybe, just like you two,

18:05.220 --> 18:09.570
Ai Hoshino had been reincarnated and was 
somewhere out there living a happy life?

18:09.570 --> 18:10.870
Nope.

18:12.250 --> 18:15.990
Ai Hoshino's story 
ended right then and there.

18:15.990 --> 18:18.820
Utterly and thoroughly.

18:20.040 --> 18:26.170
Her soul crumbled into pieces and 
returned to the stars and the sea.

18:26.480 --> 18:29.510
Never will it take shape again.

18:32.370 --> 18:34.050
Death is final.

18:36.190 --> 18:41.230
Ai Hoshino will no longer 
think or feel anything.

18:41.680 --> 18:46.190
She'll never smile again, 
no matter what you do.

18:47.530 --> 18:49.900
Did you tell Ruby the same thing?

18:49.900 --> 18:51.860
Ooh, scary!

18:52.470 --> 18:57.820
I don't have to. She'll come 
to fulfill her role one day.

18:58.640 --> 19:02.440
You should give some more thought, too,

19:03.110 --> 19:06.490
as to why your soul 
was carried into that body.

19:13.220 --> 19:14.940
I don't need you to remind me.

19:16.140 --> 19:20.680
There's only one reason 
I was born into this life—

19:21.060 --> 19:22.590
only one purpose.

